Enact Holdings, Inc. is a subsidiary of Genworth Holdings Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rohit  Gupta | President, CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 419 people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $45K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Enact Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.1B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 7% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 18\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 8.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 81% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $167.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 44% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Does Quarterly Earnings Change The Bull Case For Enact Holdings (ACT)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-act/enact-holdings/news/does-quarterly-earnings-change-the-bull-case-for-enact-holdi","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794486536.478,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.719,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Enact Holdings (ACT) Stock Dropped, So What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-act/enact-holdings/news/enact-holdings-act-stock-dropped-so-what-is-driving-attentio","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794216470.606,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.888,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Enact Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ:ACT) Third-Quarter Results Are Out And Analysts Have Published New Forecasts","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-act/enact-holdings/news/the-enact-holdings-inc-nasdaqact-third-quarter-results-are-o","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794058584.648,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"s